  "notes": [
    "Deck is titled 'ORANGE COUNTY | AUGUST 2026 HOUSING MARKET UPDATE' and is the 'City Data Only' cut: 13 OC cities, no national/macro section, no Reports-on-Housing reduction breakdown.",
    "DATA IS GENUINELY FRESH versus the July 28 2026 deck. Sold slides advance from 'JUNE 2026 SOLD' to 'JULY 2026 SOLD' with different values in every city (San Clemente 55 -> 65 homes, $1.9m -> $1.7m median), and the Zillow section advances from 'May 2026 Home Prices' to 'June 2026 Home Prices'. Verified by diffing pdftotext -layout output of both decks. Unlike the July 28 deck, nothing here is recycled.",
    "Per-city comparison slides are titled 'Year-Over-Year Comparison'. The overview 'Y-O-Y CHANGES' column and per-city deltas are YEAR-OVER-YEAR and are stored in the legacy inventory_mom_pct / pending_mom_pct / emt_mom_days fields to preserve the pipeline; for THIS deck those legacy-named fields hold Y-o-Y values.",
    "GOTCHA - North Coastal Area slide, Corona Del Mar row: reads '82 Homes / 32 Pendings / 77 Days / +39% | +60% | -12 Days', which is Aliso Viejo's row duplicated. The main overview slide and the per-city Corona Del Mar slide both read 74 / 11 / 202 days (Last Year 182). Internal math confirms: 74 / (11/30) = 202. Using 74 / 11 / 202.",
    "GOTCHA - North Coastal Area slide, Newport Beach row: reads '-20% | +31 Days', which is Laguna Niguel's demand and EMT delta. The main overview and the per-city Newport Beach slide both read '-6% or -3 Pending' and 'Last Year: 148 Days' (163 - 148 = +15). Using -6% / +15 days.",
    "GOTCHA - South Coastal Area slide, Laguna Niguel row: EMT reads '163 Days', which is Newport Beach's EMT. The main overview and the per-city Laguna Niguel slide both read 129 days, and the math confirms it: 168 / (39/30) = 129. Using 129.",
    "GOTCHA - price-reduction percentages: the per-city slides are shifted by one position from Laguna Beach onward (per-city Laguna Beach shows 44% = Laguna Niguel's value, per-city Laguna Niguel shows 40% = Newport Beach's, per-city Newport Beach shows 32% = Newport Coast's, per-city Newport Coast shows 44% = San Clemente's, per-city San Clemente shows 45% = San Juan Capistrano's). The main Active Price Reductions slide and both regional reduction slides agree with each other on all 13 cities, so the aggregates are used: Laguna Beach 42, Laguna Niguel 44, Newport Beach 40, Newport Coast 32, San Clemente 44, San Juan Capistrano 45. NOTE: San Clemente is 44%, not the 45% printed on its own slide.",
    "GOTCHA - Costa Mesa ALL sold S/L ratio: the per-city slide reads 91.1%. The aggregate slide reads 99.1%, and since all 46 Costa Mesa sales were under $5M the ALL and $0-5M buckets must match (the $0-5M bucket reads 99.1% on both slides). Using 99.1%.",
    "GOTCHA - Irvine $5M+ sold count: the per-city slide reads '55 HOMES SOLD'. The aggregate slide reads 5, and 171 + 5 = 176 ALL. Using 5.",
    "GOTCHA - San Clemente bucket split: the per-city slide reads 65 under $5M and 2 above $5M, which sums to 67 against an ALL count of 65. The aggregate slides read 64 and 1, which sums correctly. Using 64 / 1. The per-city $0-5M S/L of 100.4% is likewise the ALL figure bleeding in; the aggregate reads 100.3%.",
    "GOTCHA - Corona Del Mar Zillow Y-o-Y: the main Home Price Snapshot slide reads '+86%'. The North Coastal slide reads '+8.6%'. Using +8.6%.",
    "EMT math verified against inventory / (demand / 30) for all 13 cities after corrections; every city reconciles to within rounding.",
    "Orange County aggregate: Zillow HVI June 2026 0.0% M-o-M, +1.7% Y-o-Y, +91.7% 10-yr; 41% of OC inventory carries a price reduction. No Reports on Housing reduction breakdown in this deck cut - the July 28 file's breakdown (as of 2026-07-01) remains the most recent."
  ],
